title: Proposition 29
---
order: 29
---
short_label: XI.29
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Parallelepipedal solids which are on the same base and of the same height, and in which the ends of their edges which stand up are on the same straight lines, equal one another.
----
proof:

Let {CM} and {CN} be parallelepipedal solids on the same base {AB} and of the same height, and let the ends of their edges which stand up, namely {AG}, {AF}, {LM}, {LN}, {CD}, {CE}, {BH}, and {BK}, be on the same straight lines {FN} and {DK}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="300" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
